# Keep the build context clean.
#
# This file exists because of a real failure: `COPY backend/ ./` swept the
# developer's local `backend/.env` into the production image. pydantic-settings
# reads that file for any setting the container environment does not explicitly
# define, so the API silently inherited CELERY_TASK_ALWAYS_EAGER=true,
# PROVIDER=linkedin and a Windows PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH — and ran scrape jobs
# itself instead of queueing them for the recruiter's laptop.
#
# Two consequences, both bad: production behaviour decided by a file nobody
# thought was deployed, and any secret in it baked into a shippable image.

# --- Secrets. Never in an image. ---
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Local databases: real candidate PII ---
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Python build artefacts ---
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
.venv
venv

# --- Node / Next.js (the web image builds from ./frontend) ---
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo

# --- Scraper local state. Machine-specific; must not travel. ---
.pw-browsers
backend/_debug
backend/_state
storage-state

# --- Documents and editor noise ---
*.pdf
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.mcp.json
